  "notes": "Two related but distinct reportable consequences are chained sequentially: (1) 22 SGFP coupling failure -> manual trip [50.72(b)(2)(iv)(B)], and (2) subsequent 21 SGFP trip during post-trip recovery -> loss of MFW / AFW actuation [50.72(b)(3)(iv)(A)]. Official cause code B applies to the root piping-strain/misalignment cause of the 22 SGFP coupling failure; the 23 SGFP STOP/LOCKOUT unavailability is modeled as a contributing FailureMode in the chain per the narrative's 'underlying cause' language rather than as a second Cause node, since block 13 lists a single cause code. AFW modeled as BACKED_UP_BY since narrative states it was manually initiated and restored feedwater successfully. MFW/RTO design details and Ovation system are design context, not modeled as separate System nodes. Manufacturer code B580 carried from block 13 with no further identification given in narrative."
